Z||000000||JetroGT||02-12-2000||02:09 AM||||<BR>I noticed in my 87 GT that their is no floor lights installed. Is it possible to take the wiring from an 86 and just plug it in? <BR>I just wanted it because it looks better. When you open the door the whole inside of the car lights up alot better.||||reg||1
Z||000001||AL||02-12-2000||02:14 AM||||are you sure?there should be a light by the fuse boxs and on the passenger side under the dash, maybe your lights need to be replaced.||||reg||1
Z||000002||batboy||02-12-2000||08:56 AM||||Al, actually that was an optional lighting package that also included a light in the trunk too, in addition to the two "floor" lights. It shouldn't be too tough to do if you have the whole donar car to work with. I like having the extra interior lights.||||reg||1
Z||000003||David Gamache||02-12-2000||11:44 AM||||The floor lights are a orange and white two wire harness that simply plugs in above the fuse block.||||reg||1
